<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balambangan Island</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1775</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balambangan Island is an island off the northern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a>, Malaysia. In 1773 the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> founded a trading post there, intended to tap the trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the Sulu and Malay worlds. In 1775 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tausug">Tausug</a> warriors attacked and destroyed the settlement; a second attempt in 1803–1805 was also abandoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balambangan-island.jpg" alt="Balambangan Island" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cccefalon; Pushpin: McSush · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SouthernPartofSabah-Scheme-PulauBalambangan_Pushpin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
